\name{cellucid_filter_continuous_reset}
\alias{cellucid_filter_continuous_reset}
\title{Reset a visible range}
\usage{
cellucid_filter_continuous_reset(viewer, field)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{The continuous field or gene the view in focus is colored by, by name. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Show every value of a continuous field or gene again.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{filter.continuous.reset} (Filters). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{filters}, \code{colors}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_filter_continuous_reset(viewer,
      field = list(key = "cell_type", source = "obs"))
